<title>HONG KONG: China mulls HK office to handle forex reserves - TV.</title>
<headline>China mulls HK office to handle forex reserves - TV.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's central bank, the People's Bank of China, is considering setting up an office in Hong Kong to deal with the country's foreign reserves, Hong Kong television reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The move could boost the mobility and value of China's reserves, Hong Kong television quoted the bank's deputy governor Chen Yuan as saying after a conference staged by the Hong Kong Monetary Authority and International Monetary Fund.</p>
<p>China's foreign exchange reserves amounted to US$110 billion at the end of February.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
